cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "MARLauder: GPU-resident multi-agent RL for cooperative exploration under intermittent communication"
message: "If you use this software, please cite the accompanying paper."
type: software
# Authors are withheld for double-blind review. Fill in before a public release.
authors:
  - name: "Anonymous"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://example.org/marlauder"
abstract: >-
  A GPU-resident multi-agent reinforcement learning system for cooperative exploration of unknown
  occupancy maps under intermittent, signal-strength-limited communication. Robots maintain private
  maps and a learned belief over teammate positions, and are trained with MAPPO using a
  count-invariant CTDE critic, a privileged team-union exploration reward, and a sync-event reward
  that pays for the map actually exchanged at a rendezvous.
keywords:
  - multi-agent reinforcement learning
  - robotic exploration
  - graph neural networks
  - MAPPO
